cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This file cites the research software repository as a whole (project-level
  version 0.1.0). To cite the reproducibility package of the study "When Does
  LLM-Serving Scheduler Adaptation Matter? Action Opportunity and Causal
  Headroom in Production-Derived Replay", cite its Zenodo record instead,
  listed under references: version 1.1.0,
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22866983 (the concept DOI
  10.5281/zenodo.22865293 resolves to the latest version).
type: software
title: "llm-serving-heuristic-evolution"
abstract: >-
  Research code for measuring when changing an LLM-serving scheduler creates an
  actionable opportunity: a discrete-event serving simulator, scheduling
  policies, production-derived trace replay, scheduler-disagreement detection,
  one-step counterfactual latency headroom, and a bounded real-vLLM probe.
